          "note": {
            "Ukeverk": [
              "From July 2025 onward, the trend figures for man-weeks worked by men in the LFS show a marked increase, without a corresponding rise in the number of employed persons. This is because the seasonal adjustment model treats July as an outlier with a level shift for hours worked by men, and as a near outlier for men present at work. In the LFS, a week is assigned to the month in which the Thursday falls. According to this rule, July 2025 contained five weeks, something that last occurred in 2021. Our analysis also shows that men and women took their summer holidays at different times in 2025. This, combined with July having five weeks, has affected the seasonal adjustment."
            ]
          }
